{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/65108-attributes-skills-and-pacts","id":65108,"title":"Attributes, Skills, and Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-04T13:49:14-08:00","id":65108,"title":"Attributes, Skills, and Pacts","content":"Two Questions:<br /> <br /> 1. The book states that increasing Attributes with Pacts is possible, but no systems are presented in the book. Is this something that will be addressed in a later book, or was there just an accident in it being left out?<br /> <br /> 2. Does the Skill Pact Asset actually add to the character's rating, or is it more like an equipment bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T15:23:14-08:00","id":65181,"title":"","content":"#2 first, as far as I can tell, Skill pact adds to the targets skill dots, but it's worded very ambiguously to my mind, so I could easily see it being interpreted the other way. My opinion on this is mostly supported by the last sentence in the Skill pact section, which refers to them as Bonus Dots, and being able to take a human past Five Dots.<br /> <br /> #1 is harder, but the current thinking, at least as I have seen, is that granting Attributes was part of an earlier build of the Pact system, and that various references (such as stating that you could grant a mortal health by increasing her stamina) are anachronisms/artifacts of that earlier build that should have been written out, but didn't get pulled. It's worth noting that under GMC and DtD rules, Merits are 1xp per dot, Skills 2xp per dot, and Atts 4xp per dot. So, it might be feasible to allow +1 Attribute as a Greater (+3 pact weight) benefit, but it's not actually in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T15:26:20-08:00","id":65187,"title":"","content":"I get a mixed message from the Skill section for pacts mainly due to this part <br /> <br /> Skill <br /> benefits come in lesser, medial and greater varieties, corresponding <br /> to a 1-, 2-, and 3-die bonus to the Skill in question, respectively. A <br /> 1-point Skill benefit can also grant a specialty. These bonus dots can <br /> take a Skill above the human maximum of five dots.<br /> <br /> making it sound like a die bonus and then the next sentence like actual dots in the Skill, personally I'm going to treat them like dots in the skill. <br /> <br /> As for Attributes I think a medial pact(2-point) would work for 1 dot in an attribute and a greater pact (3-point) would allow 2 dots in a single attribute or a 5 dot attribute to 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2001-tyler-foss","name":"Tyler Foss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}